Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

18 plates were registered and one was mounted, so there was no way to look at
the other 17 without reading the registry. That is a gap in the process, not in
the work: P0 was 'homepage only, ship that PR', and the mounting maps for P1 and
P2 are still ahead.

Noindex, unlinked, baselined in links-baseline.json with the reason. It is a
review surface, not a gallery — the briefs are explicit that a second gallery is
not wanted and that three sliders on ranking pages beat sixteen on pages nobody
opens. Each card prints the plate id, which archive its frames came from, and
the routes it is destined for, so the page doubles as the mounting worksheet.

Delete it once the placements are done.

