Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(proof): mount every plate on the pages the registry
 assigns it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

P0 shipped one slider on the homepage and stopped, because that is what the
briefs called P0. That left 17 plates registered, bundled, verified and visible
nowhere, which is not "done" by any reading — the placement maps were in the
brief from the start.

THE MOUNT IS DATA, NOT FIFTEEN DECISIONS

Every plate already carries its own `routes` list: that is the placement map,
already in the registry. So ProofSliderForRoute takes a route and asks the
registry which plates belong there, and a page says where it is rather than
which pictures it wants. One line per page. Moving a plate between pages is now
a registry edit, not a hunt through fifteen files.

It renders nothing when a route has no plate, which is what makes it safe on
/service-areas/[city] — thirty-two cities, six of which have a slider.

WHAT THAT REACHES

Three dynamic route files carry eleven placements on their own:

  /case-studies/[slug]     5 case studies that had never published an image
  /service-areas/[city]    forest-hill, midtown-toronto, richmond-hill,
                           rosedale, yorkville
  /services/[slug]         dust-free-sanding

Nine static pages carry the rest: /commercial, /guides, /realtors, /services,
/service-areas, and the four head terms — refinishing, flooring, stairs and
problems.

The homepage keeps its single hero slider from the P0 commit rather than the
three the registry lists for '/', because a homepage is not a carousel.

The internal review page from the previous commit is deleted in the same breath.
It existed to look at plates that were not mounted; they are mounted, so it is
scaffolding, and scaffolding that survives a build becomes a second gallery
nobody asked for.

Nothing was removed from any page. Every slider is an addition above the
existing copy, and EvidenceRail, JobCardRail and PricingSection are untouched.

50 guards green. tsc at the 107-error Prisma sandbox baseline.

